From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:12:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: pm8998: add the PMIC watchdog

The PM8998 PON block has the PMIC watchdog that pm8916_wdt drives, with
its bark on PON interrupt 6. Only the power-off reason registers differ,
hence the qcom,pm8998-wdt compatible in front of the PM8916 fallback.

Its bite resets the PMIC directly, without going through the secure world.
That matters on SDM845 devices whose TZ does not reset on an APSS watchdog
bite. Leave it disabled, so boards opt in.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi
index 3ecb330590..8fdba4a3e5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi
@@ -59,6 +59,12 @@ pm8998_resin: resin {
 				bias-pull-up;
 				status = "disabled";
 			};
+
+			pm8998_wdt: watchdog {
+				compatible = "qcom,pm8998-wdt", "qcom,pm8916-wdt";
+				interrupts = <0x0 0x8 6 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
 		};
 
 		pm8998_temp: temp-alarm@2400 {
